## PART 1: PREREQUISITES & SETUP

### Step 1: Install Required Software

#### Windows Users:
1. **Download Java Development Kit (JDK)**
   - Go to: https://www.oracle.com/java/technologies/downloads/
   - Download JDK 11 or later
   - Install it (remember the installation path)

2. **Download Android Studio**
   - Go to: https://developer.android.com/studio
   - Download and install Android Studio
   - Run Android Studio and complete the setup wizard
   - Install Android SDK (API 33 or higher)

3. **Download Node.js**
   - Go to: https://nodejs.org/
   - Download LTS version
   - Install it

4. **Download Git**
   - Go to: https://git-scm.com/download/win
   - Install Git

#### Mac Users:
```bash
# Install Homebrew first if not installed
/bin/bash -c "$(curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Homebrew/install/HEAD/install.sh)"

# Install Java
brew install openjdk@11

# Install Node.js
brew install node

# Install Git
brew install git

# Download Android Studio from https://developer.android.com/studio
```

#### Linux Users:
```bash
# Ubuntu/Debian
sudo apt-get update
sudo apt-get install openjdk-11-jdk
sudo apt-get install git
curl -o- https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nvm-sh/nvm/v0.39.0/install.sh | bash
nvm install node

# Download Android Studio from https://developer.android.com/studio
```

### Step 2: Set Environment Variables

#### Windows:
1. Open `System Properties` → `Environment Variables`
2. Add new System Variables:
   ```
   JAVA_HOME = C:\Program Files\Java\jdk-11.0.x (your JDK path)
   ANDROID_HOME = C:\Users\YourUsername\AppData\Local\Android\Sdk
   ```
3. Add to PATH:
   ```
   %JAVA_HOME%\bin
   %ANDROID_HOME%\tools
   %ANDROID_HOME%\tools\bin
   %ANDROID_HOME%\platform-tools
   ```

#### Mac/Linux:
Add to `~/.bash_profile` or `~/.zshrc`:
```bash
export JAVA_HOME=$(/usr/libexec/java_home -v 11)
export ANDROID_HOME=$HOME/Library/Android/Sdk
export PATH=$PATH:$ANDROID_HOME/tools:$ANDROID_HOME/tools/bin:$ANDROID_HOME/platform-tools:$JAVA_HOME/bin
```

Then run:
```bash
source ~/.bash_profile  # or ~/.zshrc
```

### Step 3: Verify Installation

Open terminal/command prompt and run:
```bash
java -version
node --version
npm --version
git --version
adb devices  # This should list Android devices
```

